            <ArticleTitle>[Failures in enosseous impantations].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>302-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It was possible to examine over 500 jaw implants which were anchored in bone after varying duration of wear. The average failure rate of these implants after up to seven years after insertion lies approximately 40% above the complication rate given in the majority of publications. The time of occurrence and the symptoms of failures are discussed as well as their possible causes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
